"""ARCH-41 Tranche 1 — Redaction Studio seams, automation conformance, backup floor.

Run from backend/:

    python apply_arch41.py --check      # report every file, write nothing
    python apply_arch41.py              # apply
    python apply_arch41.py              # again: every line reads "already applied"
    python apply_arch41.py --rollback   # restore what the last apply replaced
    python apply_arch41.py --list       # the files this script owns

ARCH41-S1:apply. GENERATED from the real diff against `2f81cdf` ("Production
Hardening Phase") by gen_apply_arch41.py, which refuses to emit if any file
carries no ARCH41-S1 sentinel.

THE ENGINE IS ARCH-40's, UNCHANGED IN SHAPE
===========================================

Each operation names:

  final_sha    sha256 of the ARCH-41 result              -> "already applied"
  accepted     sha256 of the 2f81cdf baseline file       -> replaced
  anything else, unless a later milestone
  (ARCH-42 onward) has already edited the file           -> REFUSED, nothing written

Hashes are over normalised text (BOM stripped, CRLF -> LF), so a Windows
checkout hashes the same as a Linux one; writes keep each file's own newline
style, BOM and (on POSIX) permission bits — deploy/bin/flowpilot-sweep must
stay executable.

Everything is validated before anything is written. Each write goes to a
temporary file and is renamed into place; a failure restores every file this
run already wrote. Originals are kept under backend/.arch41_apply_backup/<ts>/.

Tranche 1 adds NO migration. The Alembic head stays
arch40_step2a_review_view_paths.

9 files: 5 new, 4 replaced.
"""

